  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_010 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, imagenet_vit_l, transformer agg, weighted fusion) achieved 0.520 acc, a large jump over config_012 (same but singleprofile, no aggregation) at 0.422. This gain is attributed to the combination of multiprofile + transformer aggregation, but we cannot yet tell whether the transformer is specifically critical or whether any aggregation of multiple profiles would suffice. Question: config_018 changes only the aggregation from transformer to avgpool while holding all other settings identical to config_010, cleanly isolating the aggregation method. Why this is the best next experiment: it is a single-variable comparison against our strongest result, directly testing whether the transformer's learned attention over profiles is the key mechanism or whether simpler pooling captures most of the multiprofile benefit. This mechanistic insight will determine whether subsequent experiments should prioritize transformer-based designs or whether we can redirect budget toward other untested variables (RNA encoder, image encoder, fusion method) with a simpler aggregation."
}

